From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 18:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: h713: drive the accelerometer with mainline st_accel

TWI1 (PH2/PH3) carries the projector's tilt sensor, which stock uses for
keystone. The dtsi copied stock's children verbatim: an "stk,stk83xx" node
named stk8ba58@18 plus kxtj3, mir3da and lsm6dsr alternatives. None of those
compatibles has a mainline driver, and the board DTS kept the bus disabled.

The chip at 0x18 is not an STK8BA58. The U-Boot scan of this bus answers only
at 0x18, and stock's register dump of that device reads WHO_AM_I (0x0f) =
0x11 with LIS3DH-style CTRL_REG1 = 0x37 (25 Hz, XYZ on) and CTRL_REG4 = 0x98
(BDU, +/-4 g, high resolution) at 0x20/0x23. That is a Silan SC7A20, a LIS3DH
clone, and stock's stk83xx driver is a multi-chip one with an sc7a20_reset
attribute. Its reading at rest, 1264,272,-8144 left-justified at +/-4 g, is
about -1 g on Z.

Mainline st_accel binds "silan,sc7a20" and checks that same WHO_AM_I, so
replace the vendor children with one node and enable the bus on the board. The
sensor then appears as a standard IIO device (in_accel_{x,y,z}_raw/_scale).

No interrupt is wired: stock lists an irq-gpio, but polled sysfs reads need
none and its pin is not yet mapped.

The mount-matrix was measured on the board by standing the projector lens-up
(chip +Y read +0.98 g), level (chip Z read -1.03 g) and right side raised (chip
X read -0.6 g). It maps the chip onto the IIO device frame as seen from behind
the projector: X right, Y up, Z back toward the viewer, so a level projector
reads +1 g on Y and a ceiling mount reads -1 g.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -764,32 +764,27 @@
 			#size-cells = <0>;
 			status = "okay";
 
-			/* Stock TWI1 children (from live DTS dump) */
-			stk8ba58@18 {
-				compatible = "stk,stk83xx";
+			/*
+			 * Stock names this "stk8ba58" and lists kxtj3, mir3da
+			 * and lsm6dsr alternatives for other builds. Only 0x18
+			 * answers on this board, and stock's register dump of
+			 * it reads WHO_AM_I (0x0f) = 0x11 with a LIS3DH-style
+			 * CTRL_REG1..4 at 0x20: a Silan SC7A20, which mainline
+			 * st_accel drives. Stock's own driver is a multi-chip
+			 * one with an sc7a20_reset attribute.
+			 */
+			accelerometer@18 {
+				compatible = "silan,sc7a20";
 				reg = <0x18>;
-				status = "okay";
-				stk,direction = <2>;
-				stk,prj_pianzhou = <1>;
-				stk,swipe_xy = <0>;
-			};
-
-			kxttj3@e {
-				compatible = "kxtj3";
-				reg = <0x0e>;  /* stock: name @18 but reg=0x0e */
-				status = "disabled";
-			};
-
-			da228ec@27 {
-				compatible = "mir3da";
-				reg = <0x27>;  /* stock: name @0e but reg=0x27 */
-				status = "okay";
-			};
-
-			lsm6dsr@6a {
-				compatible = "lsm6dsr";
-				reg = <0x6a>;
-				status = "disabled";
+				/*
+				 * Projector frame, viewed from behind it: X right,
+				 * Y up, Z back toward the viewer (the lens is -Z).
+				 * Measured 2026-10-06: up = chip -Z, lens = chip +Y,
+				 * right = chip -X.
+				 */
+				mount-matrix = "-1",  "0",  "0",
+					        "0",  "0", "-1",
+					        "0", "-1",  "0";
 			};
 
 			/*
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@
 &cpu_comm_reserved { status = "okay"; };
 &mips_framebuf { status = "okay"; };
 &framebuf_reserved { status = "okay"; };
-&twi1 { status = "disabled"; };
+&twi1 { status = "okay"; };
 &codec { status = "okay"; };
 &dummy_cpudai { status = "disabled"; };
 &codec_machine { status = "disabled"; };
-- 
